From ee9a3f6376d5ccf6276d26b2cde5b72ad62fc05c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Jonathan D.A. Jewell" <6759885+hyperpolymath@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:28:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Report what a clr_lm replacement imputed, not only the
 worst sample

`diagnostics.zero_replacement` gains `via` (which code produced the numbers:
`zCompositions::multRepl`, the Julia reference, or nothing, because a table
with no zeros needs no replacement), the median and count over 10% of the
imputed share, and the size of the composition. The summary line under a
`clr_lm` result now says what the estimate is a difference of - min_prevalence
chose the taxa the log-ratios are taken over, and it is the same number that
kept the imputed mass small - and quotes the median share next to the maximum,
because "at most X%" on its own reads like an all-clear for a table where every
sample is mostly imputed.

The sentence is `zeroReplacementLine`, in `differentialTable.ts` beside
`configLine` and `effectValue` so it is tested rather than rendered.

Refs #25
